<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The window behind the app, which is what shows between the launcher and the
        first composition, and which Android 12 and up also draws the splash icon
        on.

        The icon's own cream, so that on a light phone the splash and the icon are
        one surface and there is no seam between them. values-night/ answers the
        other half: a cream window on a dark phone is the white flash this setting
        exists to prevent, and it is the reason this colour is separate from
        ic_launcher_background at all — the icon may not follow the system theme,
        and this must.
    -->
    <color name="splash_background">#F3EDE3</color>
</resources>
